{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Thorns.</b> Greater and lesser than it is דרדר, and it alone has a [root] basis of ד-ר, for its brothers are missing [root letters]." "And the sense of 'in toil' is to plow and to harrow and to sow, and further an evil consequent: that thorns grow among the grain." "And the sense of 'the herb of the field' — it is bread. For in the Garden, his sustenance was from the fruit of the tree."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:03.415514401Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}